.TH c++filt 1 "February 2026" "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
c++filt \- demangle Itanium, Rust, and D symbol names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B c++filt
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ mangled-name ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B c++filt
is a command-line wrapper around
.BR libdemangle .
It reads mangled names from arguments or standard input and prints demangled forms.
.PP
Supported mangling schemes:
Itanium C++ ABI (
.B _Z
prefix), Rust (
.B _R
and legacy Rust patterns), and D (
.B _D
prefix).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-s, --style " style
Select style: auto, gnu-v3, itanium, rust, dlang, none.
.TP
.B -n, --no-strip-underscore
Do not strip a leading underscore.
.TP
.B -_, --strip-underscore
Strip one leading underscore before demangling.
Only the stripped name is tried: a name that does not demangle without
its first underscore, such as
.BR _Z3foov ,
is printed unchanged.
.TP
.B -p, --no-params
Omit function parameter types.
.TP
.B -t, --types
Attempt bare type demangling.
.TP
.B -i, --no-verbose
Suppress verbose qualifiers where supported.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print
.B demangle_version()
string.
.SH INPUT MODES
If one or more operands are provided, each operand is treated as one input name.
Otherwise,
.B c++filt
reads stdin line-by-line and demangles embedded mangled tokens.
A token is a whole word: a maximal run of letters, digits,
.BR _ ,
.BR $ ,
and
.BR . .
A word is demangled only as a whole; a mangling prefix such as
.B _Z
in the middle of a word (for example
.BR FOO_Z3bar )
does not start a symbol, and the word is copied unchanged.
.PP
With
.BR -t ,
every word is a candidate, in standard-input mode as in operand mode:
a bare type encoding such as
.B i
or
.B PKc
is printed as
.B int
or
.BR "char const*" ,
and a word that does not parse as a type is copied unchanged.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Option parsing error or stdin read error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR demangle (3),
.BR demangle_buf (3),
.BR nm (1),
.BR objdump (1)
